        "html_content": "\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Reorganising a Consul key-value store</title>\n    <style>\n        /* General Body Styles */\n        body {\n            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, \"Apple Color Emoji\", \"Segoe UI Emoji\", \"Segoe UI Symbol\";\n            margin: 0;\n            padding: 20px;\n            line-height: 1.6;\n            color: #333;\n            background-color: #fff;\n            font-size: 16px;\n        }\n\n        /* Container for main content */\n        .container {\n            max-width: 700px;\n            margin: 0 auto;\n            padding: 0 15px;\n        }\n\n        /* Header Navigation */\n        .header-nav {\n            text-align: right;\n            font-size: 0.9em;\n            margin-bottom: 40px;\n        }\n        .header-nav a {\n            color: #06c; /* Blue link color */\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n        .header-nav a:hover {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        /* Main Title */\n        h1 {\n            font-size: 2.5em;\n            color: #900; /* Dark red */\n            margin-top: 0;\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\n            line-height: 1.2;\n        }\n\n        /* Metadata (author/date) */\n        p.meta {\n            font-size: 0.9em;\n            color: #666;\n            margin-top: 0;\n            margin-bottom: 30px;\n        }\n        p.meta a {\n            color: #666; /* Keep author link color subtle */\n            text-decoration: none;\n            font-style: italic;\n        }\n        p.meta a:hover {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        /* General Paragraphs */\n        p {\n            margin-bottom: 1em;\n        }\n\n        /* Links */\n        a {\n            color: #06c; /* Default blue link */\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n        a:hover {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        /* Highlighted text (like WEBSERVER/ or select) */\n        .highlight-text {\n            font-weight: bold;\n        }\n\n        /* Code Blocks */\n        pre.code-block {\n            background-color: #222;\n            color: #fff;\n            padding: 15px;\n            border-radius: 4px;\n            overflow-x: auto; /* Enable horizontal scrolling for long lines */\n            font-family: \"SFMono-Regular\", Consolas, \"Liberation Mono\", Menlo, Courier, monospace;\n            font-size: 0.9em;\n            line-height: 1.4;\n            margin-bottom: 25px;\n        }\n        pre.code-block code {\n            display: block; /* Ensures padding and line-height apply correctly */\n            white-space: pre; /* Preserve whitespace */\n        }\n\n        /* Syntax Highlighting */\n        .code-block .comment { color: #666; } /* Gray for comments */\n        .code-block .keyword { color: #6cf; } /* Light blue for keywords (set, while, do, done, PUT) */\n        .code-block .option { color: #6cf; } /* Light blue for options (-e, -s, -X, -d, -r) */\n        .code-block .string { color: #6f6; } /* Green for strings (\"...\", '...') */\n        .code-block .number { color: #f66; } /* Red for numbers */\n        .code-block .variable { color: #f66; } /* Red for variables ($1, $2, $key, $value, $b64value) */\n        .code-block .function { color: #f66; } /* Red for function names (keys_and_values, set_key, migrate_to_webserver_namespace) */\n        .code-block .command { color: #6cf; } /* Light blue for commands (curl, jq, echo, base64) */\n        .code-block .path { color: #6f6; } /* Green for paths (/, A/, WEBSERVER/, /dev/null) */\n\n        /* Footnotes */\n        p.footnote {\n            font-size: 0.9em;\n            color: #666;\n            margin-top: 30px;\n        }\n        sup {\n            font-size: 0.7em; /* Smaller superscript */\n            vertical-align: super;\n            line-height: 0; /* Prevent extra line height */\n        }\n\n        /* Separator */\n        hr {\n            border: none;\n            border-top: 1px solid #eee;\n            margin: 40px 0;\n        }\n\n        /* Footer */\n        .footer {\n            font-size: 0.85em;\n            color: #666;\n            line-height: 1.5;\n        }\n        .footer p {\n            margin-bottom: 0.5em;\n        }\n        .footer a {\n            color: #06c;\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n        .footer a:hover {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        /* Responsive adjustments */\n        @media (max-width: 768px) {\n            body {\n                padding: 15px;\n            }\n            .container {\n                padding: 0 10px;\n            }\n            h1 {\n                font-size: 2em;\n            }\n            .header-nav {\n                text-align: center;\n                margin-bottom: 30px;\n            }\n            .header-nav a {\n                display: inline-block;\n                margin: 0 5px;\n            }\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <div class=\"container\">\n        <header>\n            <nav class=\"header-nav\">\n                <a href=\"#\">home</a> | <a href=\"#\">writing</a> | <a href=\"#\">TIL</a> | <a href=\"#\">now</a> | <a href=\"#\">about</a>\n            </nav>\n        </header>\n\n        <main>\n            <article>\n                <header>\n                    <h1>Reorganising a Consul key-value store</h1>\n                    <p class=\"meta\">by <a href=\"#\">David Winterbottom</a> on <time datetime=\"2017-03-27\">Monday, 27 March 2017</time></p>\n                </header>\n\n                <section>\n                    <p>If your Consul key-value store is structured as:</p>\n                    <pre class=\"code-block\"><code><span class=\"path\">/</span>\n<span class=\"path\">A/</span>\n  <span class=\"variable\">X</span> = <span class=\"number\">1</span>\n  <span class=\"variable\">Z</span> = <span class=\"number\">2</span>\n  <span class=\"variable\">Y</span> = <span class=\"number\">3</span>\n<span class=\"path\">C</span>\n<span class=\"path\">D</span></code></pre>\n\n                    <p>but you now realise you should have namespaced everything within <span class=\"highlight-text\">WEBSERVER/</span> (or something like that):</p>\n                    <pre class=\"code-block\"><code><span class=\"path\">/</span>\n<span class=\"path\">WEBSERVER/</span>\n<span class=\"path\">A/</span>\n  <span class=\"variable\">X</span> = <span class=\"number\">1</span>\n  <span class=\"variable\">Z</span> = <span class=\"number\">2</span>\n  <span class=\"variable\">Y</span> = <span class=\"number\">3</span>\n<span class=\"path\">C</span>\n<span class=\"path\">D</span></code></pre>\n                </section>\n\n                <section>\n                    <p>then this Bash script will help you migrate:</p>\n                    <pre class=\"code-block bash\"><code><span class=\"comment\">#!/bin/bash</span>\n\n<span class=\"keyword\">set</span> <span class=\"option\">-e</span> <span class=\"comment\"># Exit on error</span>\n\n<span class=\"comment\"># Emit \"key value\" lines for all keys in Consul's KV store</span>\n<span class=\"function\">keys_and_values</span>() {\n  <span class=\"comment\"># Recursively fetch all values from Consul but exclude:</span>\n  <span class=\"comment\"># (a) those that end in / (as these are folders)</span>\n  <span class=\"comment\"># (b) those that start with WEBSERVER/ (as that's where we are migrating</span>\n  <span class=\"comment\">#     to).</span>\n  <span class=\"command\">curl</span> <span class=\"option\">-s</span> <span class=\"string\">\"localhost/v1/kv/?recurse\"</span> | <span class=\"command\">jq</span> <span class=\"option\">-r</span> <span class=\"string\">'\n    .[] |\n    select(\n      ( (.Key | endswith(\"/\")) | not) and\n      (.Key | startswith(\"WEBSERVER\") | not)\n    ) |\n    [.Key, \" \", .Value] |\n    add'</span> | <span class=\"keyword\">while</span> <span class=\"keyword\">read</span> <span class=\"variable\">key</span> <span class=\"variable\">b64value</span>\n  <span class=\"keyword\">do</span>\n    <span class=\"comment\"># Consul's REST API returns values base64-encoded so we decode here.</span>\n    <span class=\"command\">echo</span> <span class=\"variable\">$key</span> `<span class=\"command\">echo</span> <span class=\"string\">\"$b64value\"</span> | <span class=\"command\">base64</span> <span class=\"option\">-d</span>`\n  <span class=\"keyword\">done</span>\n}\n\n<span class=\"comment\"># Set a new value in Consul's KV store</span>\n<span class=\"function\">set_key</span>() {\n  <span class=\"variable\">key</span>=<span class=\"variable\">$1</span>\n  <span class=\"variable\">value</span>=<span class=\"variable\">$2</span>\n  <span class=\"command\">curl</span> <span class=\"option\">-s</span> <span class=\"option\">-X</span> <span class=\"keyword\">PUT</span> <span class=\"option\">-d</span> <span class=\"string\">\"$value\"</span> <span class=\"string\">\"localhost/v1/kv/$key\"</span> &gt; <span class=\"path\">/dev/null</span>\n}\n\n<span class=\"function\">migrate_to_webserver_namespace</span>() {\n  <span class=\"function\">keys_and_values</span> | <span class=\"keyword\">while</span> <span class=\"keyword\">read</span> <span class=\"variable\">key</span> <span class=\"variable\">value</span>\n  <span class=\"keyword\">do</span>\n    <span class=\"function\">set_key</span> <span class=\"string\">\"WEBSERVER/$key\"</span> <span class=\"variable\">$value</span>\n  <span class=\"keyword\">done</span>\n}\n\n<span class=\"function\">migrate_to_webserver_namespace</span></code></pre>\n                </section>\n\n                <p>This script uses <a href=\"#\">Consul's REST API</a> and filters the results using <a href=\"#\">jq</a>.<sup>1</sup></p>\n                <p>It's easily adapted to migrate key-value pairs between different namespaces.</p>\n\n                <aside>\n                    <p class=\"footnote\"><sup>1</sup> I can never remember jq's <span class=\"highlight-text\">select</span> syntax so this post is intended largely as a personal reference on how to do this. &rarr;</p>\n                </aside>\n            </article>\n        </main>\n\n        <hr>\n\n        <footer class=\"footer\">\n            <p>Something wrong? Suggest an <a href=\"#\">improvement</a> or add a <a href=\"#\">comment</a> (see <a href=\"#\">article history</a>)</p>\n            <p>Tagged with: <a href=\"#\">consul</a>, <a href=\"#\">bash</a>, <a href=\"#\">jq</a></p>\n            <p>Filed in: <a href=\"#\">tips</a></p>\n            <nav>\n                <p>Previous: <a href=\"#\">Lies you're told on a software project</a></p>\n                <p>Next: <a href=\"#\">Podcast. init on Oscar</a></p>\n            </nav>\n            <p><small>Copyright \u00a9 2005-2023 David Winterbottom</small></p>\n            <p><small>Content licensed under <a href=\"#\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>.</small></p>\n        </footer>\n    </div>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
